---

= Pastry =

To make the pastry, sift the @plain flour{200%g} with the @salt{pinch} and @icing sugar{25%g}. Rub or cut in the @butter{100%g}(diced) until the mixture resembles fine breadcrumbs. Mix the @egg yolks{2} and @chilled water{1%tbsp}, sprinkle over the dry ingredients and mix to a dough. Knead for a few seconds until smooth. Wrap in clingfilm and chill for ~{30%minutes}.

Roll out the pastry and use to line a #23cm/9in flan tin (quiche pan){}, then chill.

= Almond Cream Filling =

Meanwhile, make the filling. Pulse the @blanched almonds{100%g} and @caster sugar{50%g} in a food processor until finely ground but not pasty. Add the @butter{65%g} and process until creamy, then mix in the @egg{1}, @egg white{1} and @almond essence{few drops}.

= Assemble and Bake =

Place a baking sheet in the oven and preheat to 190°C. Thinly peel and halve the @firm pears{3}, remove their cores and rub them lightly with @lemon juice{a little}. Put them cut side down on a chopping board and slice thinly crossways, keeping the slices together.

Pour the almond cream filling into the pastry case. Slide a palette knife under one pear half and press the top to fan out the slices. Quickly transfer to the tart, placing the fruit on the filling like spokes of a wheel. Remove a few slices from each half before arranging and use to fill in any gaps in the centre.

Place the tart on the hot baking sheet and bake for 50 to ~{55%minutes}, or until the filling is set and well browned. Cool on a wire rack.

Meanwhile, heat the @peach brandy or water{15%ml} and the @peach preserve{60%ml}(strained) in a small pan, then brush over the top of the hot tart to glaze.

> Serve at room temperature.